msgctxt "80"
msgid "What's crack-a-lacking, Kiryu-san!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "92"
msgid ""
"I, uh... Not much, Mack. You ever get that perfect shot you\r\n"
"were looking for?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "104"
msgid ""
"Can't say I did. I've been scouring every last corner of\r\n"
"this town, but all I've come up with is big fat fistfuls of nothing."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "116"
msgid "Sorry to hear that."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "128"
msgid ""
"I guess you can't expect opportunity to just fall into your\r\n"
"lap, though. Let me know if I can help."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "140"
msgid "Appreciate that to heaven and high above, Kiryu-san."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "152"
msgid ""
"Hey, by the way. You mentioned some place you wanted to\r\n"
"take me last time?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "164"
msgid "Think you can elaborate?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "176"
msgid ""
"Oh snap, Kiryu-san! That whole thing just up and slipped my\r\n"
"mind! You bet I'll elaborate!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "188"
msgid ""
"It's the hippest, swankiest, rough-and-tumblest joint this\r\n"
"side of the Sea of Japan! And yours truly just so happens to have a buddy "
"bringing home the bacon over there!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "200"
msgid "You're... saying he works there, right?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "212"
msgid ""
"Dang skippy! Oh, I almost forgot to tell you what it's called... Purgatory! "
"Kinda scary-sounding, huh?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "224"
msgid "...Did you just say Purgatory?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "236"
msgid ""
"Look, I know the name kinda gives you the heebie-jeebies,\r\n"
"but don't doubt good old Mack! I haven't breathed a sweeter\r\n"
"sip of air than when I first stepped foot in that place!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "248"
msgid ""
"Anyway, I get the feeling my perfect shot's just around the\r\n"
"corner!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "260"
msgid ""
"And by around the corner, I of course mean through some weird\r\n"
"door in a bathroom stall!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "272"
msgid ""
"Well, Kiryu-san, gotta run! I'll tell my Purgatory pal\r\n"
"you're coming, so stop by if you can muster up the courage!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "308"
msgid "Wait, Mack!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "320"
msgid "He's... something."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "332"
msgid "I guess I could swing by Purgatory when I have the time."
msgstr ""

